          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 40. \u092d\u0919\u094d\u0917\u0941\u0930\u0935\u0943\u0924\u094d\u0924\u092f\u0903\u2014evanescent or transient by nature. \u0924\u0948\u0930\u0947\u0935\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"\u091a\u093e\u092f\u0902 \u092d\u0935\u0903\u2014And wordly life ( is formed ) of them only. \u0915\u0943\u0924\u092e\u094d\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"enough with. \u0938\u092e\u093e\u0927\u0940\u092f\u0924\u093e\u092e\u094d\u2014 fix in one place. \u0915\u093e\u092e\u094b\u091a\u094d\u091b\u093f\u0924\u094d\u0924\u093f\u0935\u0936\u0947\u2014which\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"is (now) under control on account of desires being uprooted.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"\u0938\u094d\u0935\u0927\u093e\u092e\u0928\u093f\u2014in its own place or abode, viz. \u0938\u094d\u0935\u092f\u0902\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0915\u093e\u0936\u0947 \u0906\u0924\u094d\u092e\u0928\u093f.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Devanagari readings are difficult to distinguish.\"},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 41. \u0924\u0943\u0923\u0932\u0935\u0966\u2014of as little consequence as a small blade\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"of grass. \u092f\u0938\u094d\u092e\u093f\u0928\u094d\u092e\u0939\u093e\u0936\u093e\u0938\u0928\u0947\u2014V. l. Some such words as \u0932\u092c\u094d\u0927\u0947 or\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0905\u0927\u093f\u0917\u0924\u0947 \u0938\u0924\u093f should be taken as understood after this locative.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"\u092e\u0939\u093e\u0936\u093e\u0938\u0928\u0947\u2014&c.\u2014The knowledge of Brahma as expounded in the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"Upanishads; the highest truth taught by them ( the four\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"Mah\u00e1v\u00e1kyas especially ); R\u00e1marshi explains this by \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0924\u094d\u092e\u091c\u094d\u091e\u093e\u0928\u0947\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"( \u0938\u094d\u092b\u0941\u0930\u093f\u0924\u0947 \u0938\u0924\u093f ). Mr. Telang says\u2014\u201cIt means whose commands\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"are great; thus in the Upanishads \u090f\u0924\u0938\u094d\u092f \u0935\u093e \u0905\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0930\u0938\u094d\u092f \u0917\u093e\u0930\u094d\u0917\u093f \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0936\u093e\u0938\u0928\u0947\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"\u0938\u0942\u0930\u094d\u092f\u093e\u091a\u0928\u094d\u0926\u094d\u0930\u092e\u0938\u094c \u0924\u093f\u0937\u094d\u0920\u0924\u0903 \u0964 or \u092d\u0940\u0937\u093e\u0938\u094d\u092e\u093e\u0926\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0924\u0903 \u092a\u0935\u0924\u0947 &c.; the greatness consist-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"ing in the great powers which obey those commands.\u201d But\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"R\u00e1marshi\u2019s sense seems to be more natural. The knowledge of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":12,\"text\":\"Brahma is called Mah\u00e2s'\u00e2sana because it comes authoritatively\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":13,\"text\":\"from the Vedas, it being the highest truth taught by them.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":14,\"text\":\"\u0915\u094b\u093d\u092a\u093f\u2014indescribable. Cf. \u0935\u093f\u0915\u093e\u0930\u0903 \u0915\u094b\u093d\u092a\u094d\u092f\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0930\u094d\u091c\u0921\u092f\u0924\u093f \u091a \u0924\u093e\u092a\u0902 \u091a \u0915\u0941\u0930\u0941\u0924\u0947,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":15,\"text\":\"Utt. \u0928\u093f\u0924\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0926\u093f\u0924\u2014ever existing, steady, permanent. Cf. with\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":16,\"text\":\"this sl. 70 infra.; G\u00eeta VI. 22.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit and transliteration characters are indistinct.\"},\"r4\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 42. \u0930\u092e\u094d\u092f\u093e \u0938\u093e would be better for symmetry. \u0938\u093e\u092e\u0928\u094d\u0924 ( \u0938\u092e\u094d\u092f-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0903 \u0938\u092e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0903 border, frontier, \u0924\u0924\u094d\u0930 \u092d\u0935\u0903 \u0938\u093e\u092e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0903 ) means a frontier\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"king, a tributary prince. \u0935\u093f\u0926\u0917\u094d\u0927\u2014a wise man. \u0938\u093e\u092a\u093f \u0930\u093e\u091c\u092a\u0930\u093f\u0937\u0926\u094d v l.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"involves tautology since \u0938\u093e\u092e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u091a\u0915\u094d\u0930 has already occurred. \u0909\u0924\u094d\u0938\u093f\u0915\u094d\u0924\u0903\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"swollen or puffed up with pride, proud. \u0909\u0926\u094d\u0930\u093f\u0915\u094d\u0924 v. l. ( p p. of \u0930\u093f\u091a\u094d\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"with \u0909\u0926\u094d ) lit. exceeded, overflowed, hence haughty. \u0928\u093f\u0935\u0939\u2014a\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"collection. \u0938\u094d\u092e\u0943\u0924\u093f\u092a\u0925\u0917\u0924\u2014became a matter of memory i. e. history.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The divided Sanskrit word and some Sanskrit readings are unclear.\"},\"r5\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 43. \u0917\u0943\u0939\u0947\u2014used here in a double sense; (1) a house; (2) a\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"square on a dice-board. \u0924\u0924\u094d\u0930 \u092c\u0939\u0935\u0903\u2014( And there are ) many after\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"him, i. e. many who follow or depend upon him. The last two\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"lines describe the game at dice in which the god of death and\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"his wife (the male and female personifications of the principle of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"Destruction) are engaged. The world is their dice-board,\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit phrase on line 2 is indistinct.\"},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 63. )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\",\"u4\",\"u5\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"40\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"41\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r3\"]},{\"id\":\"u4\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"42\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r4\"]},{\"id\":\"u5\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"43\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"r5\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]}],\"relations\":[]}"
